Model files
-----------
glyphly downloads, on first use, two neural-network model files that are not part of
this repository:

- PP-OCRv6 small text detection and text recognition models, from PaddleOCR
  (https://github.com/PaddlePaddle/PaddleOCR), Copyright (c) PaddlePaddle Authors,
  licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0;
- in the ONNX format published by the RapidOCR project
  (https://github.com/RapidAI/RapidOCR), licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

- PP-OCRv5 mobile recognition models for other scripts (Cyrillic, Greek, Arabic,
  Devanagari, Korean, Thai, Tamil, Telugu), from PaddleOCR, Apache License 2.0, in the
  ONNX format published by RapidOCR;
- word recognition models for Indian scripts (Malayalam and others) from IndicPhotoOCR
  (https://github.com/Bhashini-IITJ/IndicPhotoOCR, MIT License, Copyright (c) 2024
  Bhashini Team@IIT Jodhpur), weights published at https://github.com/anikde/STocr under
  the Apache License, Version 2.0; converted to ONNX and int8 by glyphly
  (tools/convert_parseq.py). PARSeq architecture by Darwin Bautista and Rowel Atienza
  (https://github.com/baudm/parseq, Apache License 2.0).

glyphly's own code (detection post-processing, line straightening, decoding, word
positions, benchmark) is written from scratch.
